  "rendered_prompt": "<|im_start|>system\nYou are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\nParagraph:\n\"\"\"\nSome people believe the voting age should be lowered from 18 to 16. At sixteen, many teenagers already have jobs, pay taxes, and can drive a car. Laws about schools, the environment, and the economy will affect young people for the rest of their lives, so they should have a say in them. Critics argue that sixteen-year-olds are not mature enough to make good choices about politics. However, studies of places like Austria, where sixteen-year-olds can vote, show that young voters make choices that are just as thought-out as older voters.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer wants to use the word \"enfranchise\" in this essay.\n\nWrite 5 different sentences that use \"enfranchise\" naturally and could fit into this paragraph, on its topic and in its argument. Each sentence must contain \"enfranchise\" (another form of the word, such as a plural or past tense, is fine). Use only ideas the paragraph already contains; do not invent statistics, names or quotations. Put the best sentences first.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n",
